Nevermind about trying to dip, Valkyries start out
the game with a basic tactic of whacking most
enemies (except for certain ones with dangerous
passive attacks) upside the head with a melee
weapon.  Wizards who try that tend to die.

Then there's monks.  "Oh, awesome, a suit
of +1 Dwarvish mithril sitting on the ground
on DL2.  When I was a Tourist, wearing
mithril helped me survive so much better..."

You have to play with an awareness of role.
For someone still learning the basic features
of the game (e.g., which monsters are good
to eat), this is easier if you limit yourself (at
first) to only certain roles -- maybe not just
one role, but two or three.  Valkyrie is a
good candidate for one of your first roles,
as it tends to be easier to learn than some
of the others.  Personally I spent my first
few months of NetHack playing time on
mostly Valkyries, Tourists, and Barbarians.
Once I'd ascended a time or two, I started
adding in Knights, Monks, Rangers, and
most recently Wizards.


